Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedsparse.shoddy — reckoner seed: sparse.shoddy, converting at
Rem the bridge
Rem
Rem A sparse matrix at the keyboard is a DICT, not a cell of its own —
Rem the same call seedsimplex.shoddy made for Problem and Solution, and
Rem for the same reason. cuttle.shoddy's Cell carries a MATRIX because
Rem a dense grid is the beginner-facing form and every seed that
Rem touches one speaks it; adding a second matrix cell would put a
Rem choice in front of a reader at the moment they least want one. So
Rem a Sparse arrives and leaves as
Rem
Rem   { ("rows" n) ("cols" n) ("colix" { {r...} ... }) ("colvs" { {v...} ... }) }
Rem
Rem which DGET reads like any other dict, and which shows what the
Rem storage actually is: a row index and a value per stored entry, and
Rem nothing at all for the gaps.
Rem
Rem   SPARSE SPDENSE          across to and from a MATRIX cell
Rem   SPENTS                  build from { row col value } triplets
Rem   SPNNZ SPGET             what is stored, and one cell of it
Rem   SPCOLIX SPCOLVS         one column's row indices and values
Rem   SPCOLDOT SPMATVEC SPVECMAT SPTRANSP     the arithmetic
Rem   SPADDROW SPADDCOL       grow one
Rem
Rem NOTHING HERE ABORTS. sparse.shoddy refuses a malformed column at
Rem construction — mismatched index and value counts, an index outside
Rem the stated rows, indices that do not ascend — and a keyboard cannot
Rem afford an abort, so every one of those questions is asked here
Rem first and answered as a refusal. SpsRead is where that happens: it
Rem walks a dict cell and either hands back a Sparse known to be
Rem well formed or says which rule it broke. Nothing past it can fail.
Rem
Rem The dimension checks SpMatVec and SpVecMat make are asked here too,
Rem and so is every column index, since Nth aborts past the end of an
Rem array and reaching a column is a bare Nth by design.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "sparse.shoddy"
Include "matrix.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading arguments off the stack ---------------------------------

Def SpsEntry(k As String, v As Cell) As Cell
    CutPair(Pair(CutStr(k), v))

Def SpsNumsAt(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of Number) As Result
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        Ok(acc)
    Else
        SpsNumsNext(word, xs, acc, First(xs))

Def SpsNumsNext(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of Number, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            SpsNumsAt(word, Rest(xs), Append(acc, x))
        Case Else
            Err(RckKindWhy(word, "a LIST of NUMBERs", c), 0)

Def SpsNums(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            SpsNumsAt(word, xs, { })
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem A LIST of LISTs of numbers, which is what a column store is made of.

Def SpsRowsAt(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List) As Result
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        Ok(acc)
    Else
        SpsRowsNext(word, xs, acc, SpsNums(word, First(xs)))

Def SpsRowsNext(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(ns)
            SpsRowsAt(word, Rest(xs), Append(acc, ns))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def SpsLists(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            SpsRowsAt(word, xs, { })
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem ---- reading the dict back as a Sparse --------------------------------
Rem seeddict's shape is a LIST of CutPair cells, so this walks it by
Rem hand exactly as seedsimplex.shoddy's LpFind does rather than
Rem reaching for dict.shoddy's DictGet, which reads a different thing.

Def SpsFind(members As List Of Cell, key As String) As Cell
    If IsEmpty(members) Then
        CutBool(False)
    Else
        SpsFindAt(members, key, First(members))

Def SpsFindAt(members As List Of Cell, key As String, c As Cell) As Cell
    Select Case c
        Case CutPair(p)
            SpsFindKeyed(members, key, Fst(p), Snd(p))
        Case Else
            SpsFind(Rest(members), key)

Def SpsFindKeyed(members As List Of Cell, key As String, k As Cell, v As Cell) As Cell
    Select Case k
        Case CutStr(ks)
            If ks = key Then
                v
            Else
                SpsFind(Rest(members), key)
        Case Else
            SpsFind(Rest(members), key)

Rem The rules sparse.shoddy would Error on, asked as questions. One
Rem column: its two arrays the same length, every index a whole number
Rem inside the row count, and the indices ascending.

Def SpsColWhy(word As String, ix As List Of Number, vs As List Of Number, nr As Number, j As Number) As String
    If Length(ix) <> Length(vs) Then
        word & ": COLUMN " & Str(j) & " HAS " & Str(Length(ix)) & " INDICES AND " & Str(Length(vs)) & " VALUES"
    Else
        If Not All(ix, Fn(i) => i >= 1 And i <= nr And i = Floor(i)) Then
            word & ": COLUMN " & Str(j) & " NAMES A ROW OUTSIDE 1 TO " & Str(nr)
        Else
            If Not SpsAscends(ix) Then
                word & ": COLUMN " & Str(j) & " DOES NOT HAVE ITS ROW INDICES IN ASCENDING ORDER"
            Else
                ""

Def SpsAscends(ix As List Of Number) As Boolean
    All(Range(2, Length(ix)), Fn(k) => Nth(ix, k) > Nth(ix, k - 1))

Def SpsColsWhy(word As String, ixs As List, vss As List, nr As Number, j As Number) As String
    If j > Length(ixs) Then
        ""
    Else
        SpsColsNext(word, ixs, vss, nr, j, SpsColWhy(word, Nth(ixs, j), Nth(vss, j), nr, j))

Def SpsColsNext(word As String, ixs As List, vss As List, nr As Number, j As Number, why As String) As String
    If why <> "" Then
        why
    Else
        SpsColsWhy(word, ixs, vss, nr, j + 1)

Rem The four fields, in the shape SpsCell writes them.

Def SpsShaped(word As String, members As List Of Cell) As Result
    Select Case Pair(Pair(SpsFind(members, "rows"), SpsFind(members, "cols")),
                     Pair(SpsFind(members, "colix"), SpsFind(members, "colvs")))
        Case Pair(Pair(CutNum(nr), CutNum(nc)), Pair(CutList(ixC), CutList(vsC)))
            SpsFields(word, nr, nc, ixC, vsC)
        Case Else
            Err(word & ": NOT A SPARSE MATRIX — BUILD ONE WITH SPARSE OR SPENTS", 0)

Def SpsFields(word As String, nr As Number, nc As Number, ixC As List Of Cell, vsC As List Of Cell) As Result
    Select Case Pair(SpsLists(word, CutList(ixC)), SpsLists(word, CutList(vsC)))
        Case Pair(Ok(ixs), Ok(vss))
            SpsChecked(word, nr, nc, ixs, vss)
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def SpsChecked(word As String, nr As Number, nc As Number, ixs As List, vss As List) As Result
    If Length(ixs) <> nc Or Length(vss) <> nc Then
        Err(word & ": COLS SAYS " & Str(nc) & " BUT THERE ARE " & Str(Length(ixs)) & " COLUMNS STORED", 0)
    Else
        SpsCheckedCols(word, nr, nc, ixs, vss, SpsColsWhy(word, ixs, vss, nr, 1))

Def SpsCheckedCols(word As String, nr As Number, nc As Number, ixs As List, vss As List, why As String) As Result
    If why <> "" Then
        Err(why, 0)
    Else
        Rem Every rule sparse.shoddy would have refused has been asked,
        Rem so the record is built directly rather than through
        Rem SpFromCols, which would ask them all a second time.
        Ok(Sparse(nr, nc, ToArray(Map(ixs, ToArray)), ToArray(Map(vss, ToArray))))

Def SpsRead(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(members)
            SpsShaped(word, members)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(word & ": NOT A SPARSE MATRIX — BUILD ONE WITH SPARSE OR SPENTS", at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem ---- writing one back -------------------------------------------------

Def SpsNumList(ns As List Of Number) As Cell
    CutList(Map(ns, CutNum))

Def SpsCell(s As Sparse) As Cell
    CutList({ SpsEntry("rows", CutNum(Rows(s))),
              SpsEntry("cols", CutNum(Cols(s))),
              SpsEntry("colix", CutList(Map(Range(1, Cols(s)), Fn(j) => SpsNumList(ToList(SpColIx(s, j)))))),
              SpsEntry("colvs", CutList(Map(Range(1, Cols(s)), Fn(j) => SpsNumList(ToList(SpColVs(s, j)))))) })

Rem ---- SPARSE and SPDENSE: across to the dense grid and back ------------

Def SpsSeedAcross(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "SPARSE", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsSparse(vs)), "( matrix -- sparse )", "The same matrix stored by column, keeping only its nonzero cells. Worth it when the zeros outnumber the numbers and the grid is big; for a small full one the MATRIX is cheaper and clearer.")
    RckReg(s1, "SPDENSE", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsDense(vs)), "( sparse -- matrix )", "Back to an ordinary MATRIX, zeros and all. Exact: across and back changes nothing.")

Def SpsSparse(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case First(vs)
        Case CutMat(m)
            RckVals({ SpsCell(SpFromMat(m)) })
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(RckKindWhy("SPARSE", "a MATRIX", First(vs)))

Def SpsDense(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead("SPDENSE", First(vs))
        Case Ok(s)
            RckVals({ CutMat(SpToMat(s)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPDENSE did not answer")

Rem ---- SPENTS: from { row col value } triplets --------------------------

Def SpsSeedEnts(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "SPENTS", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsEnts(vs)), "( rows cols list -- sparse )", "Build from a LIST of { row col value } triplets. Two triplets naming one cell are added together, and a cell adding up to zero is not stored at all.")

Def SpsEnts(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckNumArg("SPENTS", Nth(vs, 1)), RckNumArg("SPENTS", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(nr), Ok(nc))
            SpsEntsAt(nr, nc, Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPENTS did not answer")

Def SpsEntsAt(nr As Number, nc As Number, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsLists("SPENTS", c)
        Case Ok(ts)
            SpsEntsWhy(nr, nc, ts, SpsTripsWhy(nr, nc, ts, 1))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPENTS did not answer")

Rem Every triplet is three whole numbers and names a cell that exists.
Rem SpFromEnts would Error on the last of those; the first two it would
Rem not notice at all, and a row index of 2.5 is not a matrix anyone
Rem meant to type.

Def SpsTripsWhy(nr As Number, nc As Number, ts As List, k As Number) As String
    If k > Length(ts) Then
        ""
    Else
        SpsTripsNext(nr, nc, ts, k, SpsTripWhy(nr, nc, Nth(ts, k), k))

Def SpsTripsNext(nr As Number, nc As Number, ts As List, k As Number, why As String) As String
    If why <> "" Then
        why
    Else
        SpsTripsWhy(nr, nc, ts, k + 1)

Def SpsTripWhy(nr As Number, nc As Number, t As List Of Number, k As Number) As String
    If Length(t) <> 3 Then
        "SPENTS: TRIPLET " & Str(k) & " HAS " & Str(Length(t)) & " NUMBERS, NOT THREE"
    Else
        If Nth(t, 1) < 1 Or Nth(t, 1) > nr Or Nth(t, 1) <> Floor(Nth(t, 1)) Then
            "SPENTS: TRIPLET " & Str(k) & " NAMES ROW " & Str(Nth(t, 1)) & ", AND THE ROWS ARE 1 TO " & Str(nr)
        Else
            If Nth(t, 2) < 1 Or Nth(t, 2) > nc Or Nth(t, 2) <> Floor(Nth(t, 2)) Then
                "SPENTS: TRIPLET " & Str(k) & " NAMES COLUMN " & Str(Nth(t, 2)) & ", AND THE COLUMNS ARE 1 TO " & Str(nc)
            Else
                ""

Def SpsEntsWhy(nr As Number, nc As Number, ts As List, why As String) As RckWork
    If why <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(why)
    Else
        RckVals({ SpsCell(SpFromEnts(nr, nc, Map(ts, Fn(t) => SpEnt(Nth(t, 1), Nth(t, 2), Nth(t, 3))))) })

Rem ---- reading one ------------------------------------------------------

Def SpsSeedRead(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "SPNNZ", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsNnz(vs)), "( sparse -- n )", "How many numbers are actually stored, as against how many cells the grid has.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "SPGET", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsGet(vs)), "( sparse r c -- n )", "The number in row r, column c — zero if nothing is stored there, which is what a gap means.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "SPCOLIX", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsColIx(vs)), "( sparse j -- list )", "Which rows column j fills, ascending.")
    RckReg(s3, "SPCOLVS", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsColVs(vs)), "( sparse j -- list )", "The values column j holds, in the positions SPCOLIX names.")

Def SpsNnz(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead("SPNNZ", First(vs))
        Case Ok(s)
            RckVals({ CutNum(SpNnz(s)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPNNZ did not answer")

Def SpsGet(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead("SPGET", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(s)
            SpsGetAt(s, RckNumArg("SPGET", Nth(vs, 2)), RckNumArg("SPGET", Nth(vs, 3)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPGET did not answer")

Def SpsGetAt(s As Sparse, r As Result, c As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(r, c)
        Case Pair(Ok(ri), Ok(ci))
            SpsGetIn(s, ri, ci)
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPGET did not answer")

Def SpsGetIn(s As Sparse, r As Number, c As Number) As RckWork
    If c < 1 Or c > Cols(s) Then
        RckWorkBad(SpsNoCol("SPGET", c, s))
    Else
        RckVals({ CutNum(SpGet(s, r, c)) })

Def SpsNoCol(word As String, j As Number, s As Sparse) As String
    word & ": THERE IS NO COLUMN " & Str(j) & " — THIS MATRIX HAS " & Str(Cols(s))

Def SpsColIx(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    SpsColumn("SPCOLIX", vs, Fn(s, j) => SpsNumList(ToList(SpColIx(s, j))))

Def SpsColVs(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    SpsColumn("SPCOLVS", vs, Fn(s, j) => SpsNumList(ToList(SpColVs(s, j))))

Def SpsColumn(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, f As [ Sparse Number -- Cell ]) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead(word, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(s)
            SpsColumnAt(word, s, RckNumArg(word, Nth(vs, 2)), f)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def SpsColumnAt(word As String, s As Sparse, j As Result, f As [ Sparse Number -- Cell ]) As RckWork
    Select Case j
        Case Ok(ji)
            If ji < 1 Or ji > Cols(s) Then
                RckWorkBad(SpsNoCol(word, ji, s))
            Else
                RckVals({ Call(f, s, ji) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Rem ---- the arithmetic ---------------------------------------------------

Def SpsSeedMath(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "SPCOLDOT", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsColDot(vs)), "( sparse j list -- n )", "Column j against a vector, touching only what is stored. This is the kernel the simplex method spends most of its time in.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "SPMATVEC", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsMatVec(vs)), "( sparse list -- list )", "The matrix times a vector, one number per row. The vector must be as long as the matrix is wide.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "SPVECMAT", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsVecMat(vs)), "( list sparse -- list )", "A vector times the matrix, one number per column. The vector must be as long as the matrix is tall.")
    RckReg(s3, "SPTRANSP", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsTransp(vs)), "( sparse -- sparse )", "The transpose: rows become columns, in one pass over what is stored.")

Def SpsColDot(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead("SPCOLDOT", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(s)
            SpsColDotAt(s, RckNumArg("SPCOLDOT", Nth(vs, 2)), SpsNums("SPCOLDOT", Nth(vs, 3)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPCOLDOT did not answer")

Def SpsColDotAt(s As Sparse, j As Result, y As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(j, y)
        Case Pair(Ok(ji), Ok(ys))
            SpsColDotIn(s, ji, ys)
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPCOLDOT did not answer")

Def SpsColDotIn(s As Sparse, j As Number, ys As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If j < 1 Or j > Cols(s) Then
        RckWorkBad(SpsNoCol("SPCOLDOT", j, s))
    Else
        If Length(ys) <> Rows(s) Then
            RckWorkBad("SPCOLDOT: THE VECTOR HAS " & Str(Length(ys)) & " NUMBERS AND THE MATRIX HAS " & Str(Rows(s)) & " ROWS")
        Else
            RckVals({ CutNum(SpColDot(s, j, ToArray(ys))) })

Def SpsMatVec(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead("SPMATVEC", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(s)
            SpsMatVecAt(s, SpsNums("SPMATVEC", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPMATVEC did not answer")

Def SpsMatVecAt(s As Sparse, x As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case x
        Case Ok(xs)
            If Length(xs) <> Cols(s) Then
                RckWorkBad("SPMATVEC: THE VECTOR HAS " & Str(Length(xs)) & " NUMBERS AND THE MATRIX IS " & Str(Cols(s)) & " WIDE")
            Else
                RckVals({ SpsNumList(ToList(SpMatVec(s, ToArray(xs)))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPMATVEC did not answer")

Def SpsVecMat(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead("SPVECMAT", Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Ok(s)
            SpsVecMatAt(s, SpsNums("SPVECMAT", Nth(vs, 1)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPVECMAT did not answer")

Def SpsVecMatAt(s As Sparse, y As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case y
        Case Ok(ys)
            If Length(ys) <> Rows(s) Then
                RckWorkBad("SPVECMAT: THE VECTOR HAS " & Str(Length(ys)) & " NUMBERS AND THE MATRIX IS " & Str(Rows(s)) & " TALL")
            Else
                RckVals({ SpsNumList(ToList(SpVecMat(ToArray(ys), s))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPVECMAT did not answer")

Def SpsTransp(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead("SPTRANSP", First(vs))
        Case Ok(s)
            RckVals({ SpsCell(SpTransp(s)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SPTRANSP did not answer")

Rem ---- growing one ------------------------------------------------------

Def SpsSeedGrow(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "SPADDROW", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsAddRow(vs)), "( sparse list list -- sparse )", "A new row on the bottom, holding the given values in the given columns. Only the columns named are touched, so a row with one number in it — a bound, a branch — costs almost nothing.")
    RckReg(s1, "SPADDCOL", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SpsAddCol(vs)), "( sparse list list -- sparse )", "A new column on the end, holding the given values in the given rows, ascending.")

Def SpsAddRow(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    SpsGrow("SPADDROW", vs, Fn(s, ix, xs) => SpsCell(SpAddRow(s, ToArray(ix), ToArray(xs))), Fn(s) => Cols(s))

Def SpsAddCol(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    SpsGrow("SPADDCOL", vs, Fn(s, ix, xs) => SpsCell(SpAddCol(s, ToArray(ix), ToArray(xs))), Fn(s) => Rows(s))

Rem Both words take the same shape of argument and break the same three
Rem rules, so they ask them once: SPADDROW's indices are columns and
Rem SPADDCOL's are rows, and the only difference is which count they
Rem have to fall inside.

Def SpsGrow(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, f As [ Sparse List List -- Cell ], lim As [ Sparse -- Number ]) As RckWork
    Select Case SpsRead(word, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(s)
            SpsGrowAt(word, s, SpsNums(word, Nth(vs, 2)), SpsNums(word, Nth(vs, 3)), f, lim)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def SpsGrowAt(word As String, s As Sparse, ix As Result, xs As Result, f As [ Sparse List List -- Cell ], lim As [ Sparse -- Number ]) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(ix, xs)
        Case Pair(Ok(ixs), Ok(vals))
            SpsGrowIn(word, s, ixs, vals, f, Call(lim, s))
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def SpsGrowIn(word As String, s As Sparse, ix As List Of Number, xs As List Of Number, f As [ Sparse List List -- Cell ], n As Number) As RckWork
    Let why = SpsColWhy(word, ix, xs, n, 1)
    If why <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(why)
    Else
        RckVals({ Call(f, s, ix, xs) })

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedSparse(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = SpsSeedAcross(RckSeeding(st, "seed-sparse"))
    Let s2 = SpsSeedEnts(s1)
    Let s3 = SpsSeedRead(s2)
    Let s4 = SpsSeedMath(s3)
    SpsSeedGrow(s4)
